Facebook Lead Ads → CRM Integration Documentation

Purpose

This document describes the complete end-to-end process for integrating
Meta (Facebook) Lead Ads with a custom CRM so that leads submitted
through Facebook Lead Forms are automatically received, enriched, and
stored in the CRM.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Prerequisites

Business Requirements

-   Meta Business Portfolio
-   Facebook Page
-   Ad Account
-   Lead Form
-   Meta Developer Account
-   CRM Backend with public HTTPS endpoint
-   Database

------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. High-Level Flow

1.  Create Meta App
2.  Complete App Settings
3.  Configure Facebook Login for Business
4.  Create Login Configuration (General + System User Access Token)
5.  Configure OAuth Redirect URI
6.  Configure App Permissions
7.  Configure Webhook
8.  Subscribe leadgen
9.  Configure Business Manager assets & Lead Access
10. Connect CRM in Business Manager
11. Submit App Review (if required)
12. Publish App
13. Test with Lead Ads Testing Tool
14. Implement Backend OAuth
15. Store Page Access Tokens
16. Receive Webhook
17. Fetch Lead Details via Graph API
18. Fetch Campaign/Ad details (optional)
19. Store lead in CRM
20. Monitor & troubleshoot

------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Meta App Setup

-   Create a Business App.
-   Link it to the correct Business Portfolio.
-   Add an App Icon, Category, Website URL, Privacy Policy URL, Data
    Deletion URL, Contact Email, Testing Instructions and other App
    Review information.
-   Publish the app after configuration.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. Permissions

Typical permissions: - leads_retrieval - pages_manage_metadata -
pages_show_list - pages_read_engagement - pages_manage_ads -
business_management - ads_read (optional for campaign insights) -
ads_management (if required)

------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. Facebook Login for Business

Enable: - Client OAuth Login - Web OAuth Login - HTTPS - Strict Redirect
URI Mode

Redirect URI: https://your-domain/api/.../facebook/callback

Create a Login Configuration: - Login Variation: General - Access Token:
System User Access Token

Generate the access token.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. Webhook

Object: Page

Callback: https://your-domain/api/.../facebook/webhook

Configure Verify Token.

Subscribe: - leadgen

Webhook must support: - GET verification (hub.challenge) - POST lead
events

------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. Business Manager

Assign Full Access to: - Facebook Page - Ad Account - Meta App

Grant Lead Access to the Page.

Verify Connected CRM contains your Meta App.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

8. App Review

Required mainly for production/external users.

Complete: - Testing Instructions - Required permissions - Business
information

------------------------------------------------------------------------

9. Lead Testing

Use Meta Lead Ads Testing Tool.

Verify: - User has Leads Permission - Lead Access Manager Enabled - User
is Page Admin

Generate test lead and confirm CRM receives it.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

10. Backend API Design

Routes: - GET /facebook/login - GET /facebook/callback - GET
/facebook/webhook - POST /facebook/webhook

Environment: - FACEBOOK_WEBHOOK_APP_ID - FACEBOOK_WEBHOOK_APP_SECRET -
FACEBOOK_WEBHOOK_REDIRECT_URI - FACEBOOK_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN -
FACEBOOK_WEBHOOK_LOGIN_CONFIGURATION_ID

------------------------------------------------------------------------

11. OAuth Flow

User → Facebook Login → Callback → Exchange authorization code →
Exchange long-lived token → Fetch pages → Store page access tokens

Validate OAuth state to prevent CSRF.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

12. Graph API Usage

Fetch Pages: GET /me/accounts

Fetch Lead: GET /{lead_id}

Useful fields: - field_data - form_id - ad_id - campaign_id -
created_time

Optional: GET /{campaign_id} GET /{ad_id}

------------------------------------------------------------------------

13. Lead Processing

Receive webhook.

Extract: - leadgen_id - page_id

Process: 1. Lookup page token 2. Fetch lead details 3. Map form fields
4. Fetch campaign/ad if required 5. Validate duplicate lead 6. Store in
CRM 7. Notify UI (optional)

Always return HTTP 200 quickly to Meta.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

14. Database Suggestions

Store: - Lead ID - Page ID - Form ID - Campaign ID - Campaign Name - Ad
ID - Lead Created Time - Raw Payload - Parsed Question/Answer Fields -
Sync Status

------------------------------------------------------------------------

15. Security

-   Environment variables only
-   HTTPS endpoints
-   Verify webhook token
-   Validate OAuth state
-   Long-lived tokens
-   Proper logging
-   API timeouts

------------------------------------------------------------------------

16. Common Problems

-   Webhook not firing → callback/subscription issue.
-   Webhook received but no lead details → missing Lead Access or
    leads_retrieval.
-   No pages → missing pages_show_list.
-   Graph API permission errors → wrong token/permissions.
-   Test lead not arriving → delete previous test lead and recreate.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

17. Production Checklist

[ ] Meta App created [ ] App settings completed [ ] OAuth configured [ ]
Permissions granted [ ] Login configuration created [ ] System User
Access Token generated [ ] Webhook verified [ ] leadgen subscribed [ ]
Business assets assigned [ ] Lead Access granted [ ] Connected CRM
verified [ ] App published [ ] Test lead successful [ ] Lead stored in
CRM [ ] Logs verified

This document is intentionally implementation-focused so it can be
reused across future projects regardless of backend framework (Node.js,
Laravel, .NET, Java, etc.).
